# What THIS repo takes from itself. The hub is a consumer of its own
# shared/config: its runners resolve .cmake-format.yaml at the repo root, like
# every consumer's do, so the root copy is a copy and can drift from the
# canonical file one directory away.
#
# Checked by the `shared-config` slug in linux/scripts/preflight.sh.
#
# One row. The other four canonical configs have NO root copy here - there is no
# C++ in this repo for the clang tools or gcovr to read, and no pre-commit
# config at the root - so they are simply not declared. That replaces the
# `--ignore .clang-format,.clang-tidy,gcovr.cfg,.pre-commit-config.yaml` this
# repo used to pass, which was the last caller of the legacy no-manifest path in
# the whole fleet. See shared/config/README.md ("The two manifests").

cmake-format
